omelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/wildmeshing/fTetWild\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">188</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":188,\"repo\":\"wildmeshing/fTetWild\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->)</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-15T16:49:26.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"nschloe/awesome-scientific-computing","categoryHTML":"<h2>Visualization</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://yt-project.org/\">yt</a> - Toolkit for analysis and visualization of volumetric data.\n(Python, BSD, <a href=\"https://github.com/yt-project/yt\">GitHub</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/yt-project/yt\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">317</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":317,\"repo\":\"yt-project/yt\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END-->)</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-15T16:49:26.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"redecentralize/alternative-internet","categoryHTML":"<h2>Networking</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://projectmeshnet.org/\">Project Meshnet</a> aims to build a sustainable decentralized alternative internet. Used by <a href=\"http://hyperboria.net/\">Hyperboria</a> and built on <a href=\"http://cjdns.info/\">CJDNS</a>.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-15T16:37:38.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"redecentralize/alternative-internet","categoryHTML":"<h2>Networking</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/skycoin/skywire\">Skywire</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/skycoin/skywire\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">57</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":57,\"repo\":\"skycoin/skywire\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> is the Skycoin Project's communication primitive (analogous to MPLS, open-flow, TOX, mesh networking, darknet, i2p) that facilitates mesh networking both on traditional internet service provider infrastructure, and on individually owned wifi and radio equipment, allowing for a phased, incentivized approach to decentralization. <a href=\"https://medium.com/skycoin/skywire-the-new-internet-for-the-new-world-6d09a8542c50\">Skywire Overview</a> | <a href=\"https://skycoin.net/\">skycoin.net</a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-15T16:37:38.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"redecentralize/alternative-internet","categoryHTML":"<h2>Uncategorised</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/cjdelisle/cjdns\">cjdns</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/cjdelisle/cjdns\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">4.8k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":4772,\"repo\":\"cjdelisle/cjdns\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> - Encrypted networking for regular people. cjdns implements an encrypted IPv6 network using public key cryptography for address allocation and a distributed hash table for routing. This provides near zero-configuration networking without many of the security and robustness issues that regular IPv4 and IPv6 networks have.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-15T16:37:38.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"redecentralize/alternative-internet","categoryHTML":"<h2>Developer tools and frameworks</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"https://github.com/orbitdb/orbit-db\">OrbitDB</a><a data-role=\"trackawesomelist-badge\" href=\"https://github.com/orbitdb/orbit-db\" style=\"text-decoration:none;top: -2px;position: relative;margin-left:4px;margin-right:4px;font-weight:400;\"><span style=\"color: #fff;font-size: 11px;font-family: Verdana, Geneva, DejaVu Sans,sans-serif;\"><span style=\"padding:4px 4px 4px 6px;background: #555;border-top-left-radius: 4px;border-bottom-left-radius: 4px;\">stars</span><span style=\"padding: 4px 6px 4px 4px;background: #007ec6;border-top-right-radius: 4px;border-bottom-right-radius: 4px;\">6.4k</span></span></a><!--TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_START____{\"type\":\"repo\",\"stargazerCount\":6432,\"repo\":\"orbitdb/orbit-db\"}____TRACK_AWESOME_REPO_ITEM_END--> is a serverless, distributed, peer-to-peer database. OrbitDB uses IPFS as its data storage and IPFS Pubsub to automatically sync databases with peers. It's an eventually consistent database that uses CRDTs for conflict-free database merges making OrbitDB an excellent choice for decentralized apps (dApps), blockchain applications and offline-first web applications.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-15T16:15:47.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"redecentralize/alternative-internet","categoryHTML":"<h2>Developer tools and frameworks</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"http://www.renderjs.org\">RenderJS</a> is a JavaScript library which provides an easy way to define gadgets (aka mashups) in pure HTML5, without requiring any application server. It is suitable for the development of mobile applications, desktop applications.</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-15T16:15:47.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"redecentralize/alternative-internet","categoryHTML":"<h2>Possibly Dead</h2>","itemHTML":"<li><a href=\"http://telehash.org/\">Telehash</a> a new encrypted P2P JSON-based protocol enabling developers to quickly build apps that are distributed and private (see the <a href=\"https://github.com/telehash/telehash.org/blob/master/protocol.md\">protocol</a> spec)</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-15T16:15:47.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"AdrienTorris/awesome-blazor","categoryHTML":"<h2>.NET Conf &#x26; Visual Studio 2022 After Party - Q&#x26;A (December 16, 2021).</h2>","itemHTML":"<li>Submit your questions for the #dotNETConf &#x26; Visual Studio 2022 After Party Q&#x26;A to #dotNET6 and #VS2022 have experts answer LIVE on <a href=\"https://twitter.com/LearnTV\">@LearnTV</a>. Submit questions by 5PM PT today and <a href=\"https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/events/learntv/dotnet-vs2022-dec-2021/\">register for free</a>: <a href=\"https://msft.it/6013k70fv\">https://msft.it/6013k70fv</a></li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-15T11:27:41.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"AdrienTorris/awesome-blazor","categoryHTML":"<h2>.NET Conf &#x26; Visual Studio 2022 After Party - Q&#x26;A (December 16, 2021).</h2>","itemHTML":"<li>December 16, 2021 | 8:30 AM - 10:00 AM PST</li>","updatedAt":"2021-12-15T11:27:41.000Z"},{"awesomeListRepo":"AdrienTorris/awesome-blazor","categoryHTML":"<h2>.NET Conf &#x26; Visual S